<!--
  **Twenty URLs: ten pages, each in two languages.**

  Every entry carries the full `hreflang` set as `xhtml:link` alternates, and that is the point of
  doing it here rather than trusting the tags `useDocumentMeta` injects. Those tags are written by
  JavaScript; these are in a static file a crawler reads before it renders anything. It is the one
  place the Ukrainian half of the site can be declared without depending on a render pass.

  Both halves of every pair declare each other, and `x-default` points at English. A one-way
  `hreflang` is ignored silently, with no warning in Search Console and no error anywhere, which is
  why `npm run check:seo` asserts reciprocity rather than leaving it to review.

  **Boards are not listed, deliberately** (P18, decision D3). All 1,000 are public and shareable; a
  blurred board behind a gate is a thin page and a thousand of them is the doorway-page pattern. The
  ten listing pages carry the content worth ranking, and `robots.txt` disallows `/game/` to match.

  The domain is hardcoded because a sitemap has to carry absolute URLs. **If the site moves to a
  custom domain, this file, `robots.txt` and the `og:image` URL in `index.html` all change
  together** — `npm run check:seo` compares them against the URL it is pointed at, so it fails
  rather than letting them drift silently.
-->
